      <abstract>
        <para>Real-time CPU scheduling in &productname; is the kernel mechanism that controls task execution timing and processor placement to provide deterministic, low-latency performance. By combining real-time policies such as <literal>SCHED_FIFO</literal> and <literal>SCHED_RR</literal> with CPU affinity through &systemd;, <command>chrt</command>, and <command>taskset</command>, administrators can eliminate thread migration overhead, preserve cache locality, and guarantee bounded dispatch latency for critical workloads.</para>
  <para><emphasis>Prerequisites</emphasis></para>
  <itemizedlist>    
    <listitem>
      <para>The <package>util-linux</package> package installed for <command>chrt</command> and <command>taskset</command></para>
    </listitem>
    <listitem>
      <para>A real-time kernel installed and running on &productname;</para>
    </listitem>
  </itemizedlist>
